condition_name: Frailty
condition_slug: frailty
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: "A physiological state characterized by increased vulnerability to stressors, Caused by decreased physiologic reserves. An endpoint of multiple disease processes"
clinical_features[3]:
  - type: Symptoms
    features[5]: Anorexia,Fatigue,Inactivity,Weakness,Weight loss
  - type: Signs
    features[6]: Abnormalities of gait and balance,Deconditioning (loss of physical functioning),Osteopenia,"Sarcopenia (decreased skeletal muscle mass, strength and exercise tolerance, thermoregulation, energy expenditure, etc.)",Slow gait speed (Timed Up and Go test ≥15 seconds),Under nutrition
  - type: Fried's phenotypic criteria for diagnosis of frailty
    features[5]: Reduced physical activity,Self-reported exhaustion/poor endurance,Slow gait,Weakness,Weight loss
investigations[6]: Full blood count,"Electrolytes, urea and creatinine",Liver function tests,Thyroid function tests,Serum calcium and albumin,Urinalysis
treatment:
  goals[1]: Return patient to baseline status
  non_drug[1]: Should be tailored to address clinical presentation
  drug[1]: Should be tailored to address clinical presentation
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[0]:
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[5]: Acute illnesses,Dependency,Disability,Falls,Hospitalizations
complications[0]:
prevention[6]: Identify patients who are pre-frail and intervene to return to robustness,Exercise (endurance and muscle strengthening; stretching and balance exercises),Nutrition (healthy food; supplements as indicated),Reduce chronic disease prevalence,Treat sarcopenia,Promote healthy aging
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null